{
  "name": "Fireflies",
  "notes": "PARTICLES THAT DO NOT MOVE, and the palette doing the work `fade` cannot. `fade` only fades OUT -- a particle is born at full weight -- so a firefly built on it would pop in and then dim, which is exactly the wrong half. So `fade` is 0 here and the envelope lives in the COLOUR: the index is age, and the palette runs black -> dim green -> bright -> amber -> black, so a particle's whole life is one traverse of it and it glows up as well as down. That is the point of `u` being the emitter's own coordinate rather than its brightness. `wrap` stays OFF, because this palette is a gradient with two ends and both of them are black -- turning it on would join them and the fade would never complete. Everything else is a near-absence of physics: `speedVary` 0.02 and no gravity, so they hang where they are born. `rate` is driven by a PERLIN LFO rather than a sine, so the field clusters and thins the way a real one does instead of breathing on a metronome.",
  "layers": {
    "0": {
      "emitter": {
        "type": "particles",
        "colouring": "age",
        "params": {
          "origin": 0.5,
          "spread": 1,
          "count": 0,
          "rate": 0.2,
          "speed": 0,
          "speedVary": 0.02,
          "acceleration": 0,
          "drag": 0,
          "size": 0.005,
          "sizeVary": 0.6,
          "softness": 1,
          "lifetime": 1,
          "lifeVary": 0.7,
          "fade": 0,
          "maxAlive": 32
        }
      },
      "colour": {
        "index": "u",
        "palette": {
          "entries": [
            "000000",
            "0a2800",
            "3f9010",
            "9fff40",
            "e8ff90",
            "6f9020",
            "0a1400",
            "000000"
          ]
        }
      },
      "blend": "add",
      "opacity": 1,
      "order": 1
    },
    "1": {
      "emitter": {
        "type": "perlin",
        "params": {
          "scale": 1.8,
          "time": 0,
          "offset": 0
        }
      },
      "colour": {
        "index": "u",
        "palette": {
